From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:43:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/win32: NIS, CAS, SGSR 1 and xBR-lv2 scalers in the
 composed present

EnhanceScaler / MESA_WSI_ENHANCE_SCALER take nis, cas, sgsr and xbr
(also "pixel"):

  nis   NVIDIA Image Scaling, its GLSL path as it is; the coefficient
        textures are constant arrays generated from NIS_Config.h; 1x to
        2x per axis (FSR 1 outside that, and for sRGB views); sharpness
        is NIS's slider; a 32x24 block per group of 128
  cas   FidelityFX CAS, sharpening and scaling in one pass
  sgsr  Snapdragon Game Super Resolution 1 with edge direction (upscaling)
  xbr   Hyllian's xBR-lv2, edge-directed scaling for pixel art, any factor

SGSR 1 and xBR-lv2 are fragment shaders: enhance/adapt.py turns copies of
them into functions the compute shaders call, at build time.  The push
constant range is 128 bytes (NIS's constants).
